WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.583 --> 00:00:06.166
Define your terms.

00:00:06.166 --> 00:00:09.708
Well, it's not a democracy in that people

00:00:09.958 --> 00:00:11.708
cannot vote for their leaders.

00:00:11.708 --> 00:00:13.583
It's not a dictatorship.

00:00:13.583 --> 00:00:17.375
Maybe that conjures up images of Hitler or Mussolini.

00:00:17.416 --> 00:00:18.750
It's not really that either.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:20.375
You have a strong leader

00:00:20.375 --> 00:00:23.291
at the top of a Communist Party or a one party state.

00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:24.875
And this leader, Xi Jinping,

00:00:24.875 --> 00:00:27.000
he doesn't have absolute power,

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.791
but he has a lot of power.

00:00:28.791 --> 00:00:30.166
It's a one party state.

00:00:30.166 --> 00:00:31.708
That may be the best way to think of it,

00:00:31.708 --> 00:00:33.708
where there's one political party

00:00:33.708 --> 00:00:37.375
that runs all facets of life, from companies

00:00:37.375 --> 00:00:40.916
to universities to the government.

00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:42.791
The term democracy is really important

00:00:42.791 --> 00:00:43.833
in Chinese politics

00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:44.750
because it goes back

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:48.291
to the beginning of modern China in 1919.

00:00:48.625 --> 00:00:50.666
There is this thing called the May 4th Movement,

00:00:50.666 --> 00:00:52.583
and people asked for Mr.

00:00:52.583 --> 00:00:54.500
Democracy and Mr. Science.

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.916
So they wanted China

00:00:55.916 --> 00:00:59.375
not to be run by emperors and things like that.

00:00:59.375 --> 00:01:01.250
But democracy means a lot of different things

00:01:01.250 --> 00:01:02.000
to different people.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:05.375
But the Communist Party claims that it's an heir

00:01:05.875 --> 00:01:10.250
to this movement and they want to cloak themselves

00:01:10.250 --> 00:01:12.958
in the mantle of this enlightened movement.

00:01:13.416 --> 00:01:16.916
So they got to say that they are a democracy,

00:01:17.208 --> 00:01:20.791
even though they are not really a democracy

00:01:20.791 --> 00:01:24.125
based on most definitions.

00:01:24.625 --> 00:01:27.000
The short answer is not really.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.791
You do have freedom of speech

00:01:28.791 --> 00:01:32.791
based on the Chinese constitution, but the scope

00:01:32.791 --> 00:01:35.708
for expressing opinion has decreased

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.500
quite a lot in recent years.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:38.041
So, you know,

00:01:38.041 --> 00:01:39.833
it used to be that you could debate

00:01:39.833 --> 00:01:41.541
a lot of different social policies.

00:01:41.541 --> 00:01:43.250
The best way to deal with

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:45.000
China's rural problems,

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.958
the best kind of economic policies

00:01:46.958 --> 00:01:48.083
that was seen as

00:01:48.083 --> 00:01:51.541
an open field for for a robust discussion

00:01:51.541 --> 00:01:52.833
on all kinds of different things.

00:01:52.833 --> 00:01:56.041
That's become a lot less in recent years, so that now

00:01:56.041 --> 00:01:58.583
the area where you can express opinions is

00:01:58.583 --> 00:01:59.541
really narrow.

00:02:01.291 --> 00:02:02.833
The Communist Party

00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:06.291
had this disaster period that when it ran China,

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:08.708
that kind of ended in the late 1970s

00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:11.541
and that included the world's worst recorded famine

00:02:11.875 --> 00:02:13.416
and a period of turmoil

00:02:13.416 --> 00:02:15.291
known as the Cultural Revolution.

00:02:15.291 --> 00:02:15.750
And China

00:02:15.750 --> 00:02:17.000
was a really poor country,

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.458
and the Communist Party had lost people's support.

00:02:19.791 --> 00:02:23.458
So they decided to try to win it back by ruling China

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:27.000
with more pragmatic policies with a lighter touch.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:30.458
They began to allow economic reforms,

00:02:30.458 --> 00:02:31.083
which has created

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.458
the prosperous superpower that we know,

00:02:33.458 --> 00:02:36.958
but they also permitted more expression of opinions

00:02:36.958 --> 00:02:41.000
and religious participation and things like that.

00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:42.875
There were always clear limits,

00:02:42.875 --> 00:02:43.791
and we can see that

00:02:43.791 --> 00:02:48.000
in 1989, with the Tiananmen Square protests

00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:51.000
that resulted in a massacre of hundreds of people

00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:53.375
because people were challenging the party.

00:02:53.375 --> 00:02:54.833
The party responded

00:02:54.833 --> 00:02:56.000
with just brute force

00:02:56.000 --> 00:02:58.166
by sending in the army and clearing the square.

00:02:58.666 --> 00:03:00.000
So that was always clear.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:03.083
But overall, there was still this scope

00:03:03.083 --> 00:03:06.958
for debate and discussion in the 1990 and 2000.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.250
And I think what happened was about 15 years ago,

00:03:10.583 --> 00:03:13.250
the party decided that things had gone too far

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.541
and they needed to rein it in.

00:03:15.541 --> 00:03:19.250
And so they started after the 2008 Beijing

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:24.750
Olympics to crack down much more seriously on dissent.

00:03:24.958 --> 00:03:27.750
People understand that the political system

00:03:27.750 --> 00:03:32.375
is run by the party and that they may be party members

00:03:32.666 --> 00:03:34.791
and they're they may therefore

00:03:34.791 --> 00:03:36.125
think they have a bit more influence.

00:03:36.125 --> 00:03:37.000
But most people,

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:37.458
let's face

00:03:37.458 --> 00:03:38.541
it, are not party members

00:03:38.541 --> 00:03:40.791
is 1.4 billion people in China.

00:03:40.791 --> 00:03:43.416
There are about 90 million party members.

00:03:43.416 --> 00:03:44.500
That's a lot of people.

00:03:44.500 --> 00:03:46.875
But that's still sort of like one in 15

00:03:46.875 --> 00:03:49.125
people are in the party.

00:03:49.125 --> 00:03:50.416
And even if you're in the party,

00:03:50.416 --> 00:03:51.833
I don't think you're going to really feel

00:03:51.833 --> 00:03:52.791
like you have a say

00:03:52.791 --> 00:03:54.500
because you can't vote on Xi Jinping

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:55.875
even if you're in the Communist Party.

00:03:55.875 --> 00:03:58.083
So there's nothing it's not like in a system

00:03:58.083 --> 00:03:59.125
that has, say,

00:03:59.125 --> 00:04:01.166
you're a member of the Republican Party

00:04:01.166 --> 00:04:02.500
or the Democratic Party

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:04.791
and you can vote in a primary

00:04:04.791 --> 00:04:06.291
for who your candidate should be.

00:04:06.291 --> 00:04:07.416
There's nothing like that in China.

00:04:07.416 --> 00:04:10.250
So I'd say basically people don't feel like

00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:11.541
they have a say.

00:04:13.166 --> 00:04:14.541
The party is fairly

00:04:14.541 --> 00:04:16.166
tolerant toward people

00:04:16.166 --> 00:04:18.625
who have constructive criticism.

00:04:18.625 --> 00:04:20.583
So if you've got a concrete problem,

00:04:20.583 --> 00:04:22.375
like let's say you're in a factory,

00:04:22.375 --> 00:04:23.666
your factory hasn't paid you

00:04:23.666 --> 00:04:26.041
for two weeks or two months or something like that,

00:04:26.291 --> 00:04:27.125
and you protest

00:04:27.125 --> 00:04:28.625
even if you protested,

00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:29.125
if the party

00:04:29.125 --> 00:04:31.041
the party would look at that and say, Aha,

00:04:31.041 --> 00:04:33.791
those people have not been paid,

00:04:33.791 --> 00:04:35.041
we're going to pay them.

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.958
We've got a big slush fund here to take care of this.

00:04:36.958 --> 00:04:38.500
We're going to just pay everybody.

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:39.041
As long as you

00:04:39.041 --> 00:04:39.833
then go home,

00:04:39.833 --> 00:04:41.833
they're going to be okay with what you did.

00:04:42.833 --> 00:04:45.500
So the party isn't against any sort of feedback.

00:04:45.500 --> 00:04:46.666
It's not like you have to completely

00:04:46.666 --> 00:04:48.583
keep your mouth closed.

00:04:48.583 --> 00:04:49.625
So I think in that sense,

00:04:49.625 --> 00:04:50.416
people may feel that

00:04:50.416 --> 00:04:52.916
they have some input in their lives,

00:04:52.916 --> 00:04:56.625
but there's no real direct way to to

00:04:56.666 --> 00:04:57.958
choose your leaders.

00:04:59.791 --> 00:05:00.041
So some of

00:05:00.041 --> 00:05:02.000
that they don't necessarily want democracy,

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:04.875
but they probably think of democracy as meaning

00:05:05.333 --> 00:05:08.041
the party listens to people and people

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:11.083
have some sort of feedback into the party.

00:05:11.458 --> 00:05:14.666
So if people feel that they aren't being listened to

00:05:14.666 --> 00:05:15.500
and this is the case

00:05:15.500 --> 00:05:17.166
with the COVID lockdowns,

00:05:17.166 --> 00:05:19.041
then they feel that that's not democratic,

00:05:19.041 --> 00:05:20.458
that's not democracy.

00:05:20.458 --> 00:05:21.958
So think of democracy

00:05:21.958 --> 00:05:26.125
maybe is more participatory as more of an interaction

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:27.083
or a dialog

00:05:27.083 --> 00:05:29.250
rather than I go to a ballot box

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.125
and vote for somebody.

00:05:31.125 --> 00:05:33.041
And I guess I guess is sort of the answer.

00:05:33.041 --> 00:05:34.166
They want to feel that

00:05:34.166 --> 00:05:38.875
they have some stable life, that they have.

00:05:38.875 --> 00:05:41.291
Tomorrow will be a better day that, you know,

00:05:41.291 --> 00:05:42.625
they'll be more prosperous,

00:05:42.625 --> 00:05:44.000
that their children can go to school

00:05:44.000 --> 00:05:44.625
and so on and so forth,

00:05:44.625 --> 00:05:46.583
just like people in every country.

00:05:46.583 --> 00:05:47.875
And they want a political system

00:05:47.875 --> 00:05:49.458
that can make that possible.

00:05:49.458 --> 00:05:52.250
And by and large, China's political system,

00:05:53.125 --> 00:05:55.375
despite its often brutal

00:05:55.916 --> 00:05:58.041
methods of governing, has delivered

00:05:58.041 --> 00:06:01.583
those kind of goods over the past 30 or 40 years.

00:06:02.375 --> 00:06:03.333
The question, I think, going

00:06:03.333 --> 00:06:03.958
forward is

00:06:03.958 --> 00:06:07.833
if it can't deliver that, then what happens?

